  "worked_solution": "Let's consider $\u25b3BCD.$ We can see that $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overset{\u2015}{CD}$ and that $CD=12\\text{\u00a0in}.$ \n\nSince the area of $\u25b3BCD$ is $42{\\text{\u00a0in}}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 42 & =\\frac{CD\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\ 42 & =\\frac{12\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\ 84 & =12\\cdot BC \\\\ BC & =\\frac{84}{12} \\\\ BC & =7\\text{\u00a0in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ is also the height of $\u25b3ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}.$ Therefore, we find the area of $\u25b3ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot BC}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{2} \\\\  & =17.5{\\text{\u00a0in}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
